{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "textDocument/didOpen", "params": {"textDocument": {"uri": "file://tests/fixtures/lsp_ws/lintgeneric/params.z", "version": 1, "languageId": "zerolang", "text": "# L023 fires: `t` is lowercase where its bound `AnyRef` is not.\nHolder: class {\n    get: function {t: this.view i: u64} outx t.view is native\n} as {\n    t: AnyRef.generic\n}\n\n# L023 fires the other way too -- the rule is a case comparison, not a\n# preference for capitals.\npair: record { a: K  b: K } as { K: anyval.generic }\n\n# L023 fires through the parenthesised default form, which a reader that\n# unwrapped only `expression` would never look inside.\nWalker: protocol {\n    Gives: AnyRef.generic\n    accepts: (AnyRef.generic default: null)\n}\n\n# NO L023: the case already matches the bound, in both families.\nKeeper: class {\n    one: function {t: this.view} outx T.view is native\n} as {\n    T: AnyRef.generic\n}\npoint: record { x: v  y: v } as { v: anyval.generic }\n\n# NO L023: a value parameter's bound is a numeric type, which is lowercase, so\n# the rule already yields a lowercase parameter with no carve-out.\nsized: record { n: u64 } as { to: u64.generic }\n\nmain: function is {\n    print \"params\"\n}\n"}}}
